No. Mutating `currentState()` in place isn't persisted. It's lost when the entity reloads, and nothing is written to the journal.

Build a new state and persist it through the effect:

```java
public Effect<Done> setName(String name) {
  var next = currentState().withName(name);   // records: return a copy
  return effects().updateState(next).thenReply(Done.getInstance());
}
```

`effects().updateState(newState)` is the only way to change a KV entity's state. Keep the state an immutable record with `withX` copy methods, so in-place mutation isn't possible.

